---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Stamp from '../components/Stamp.astro';
import { vendors, money, KLASS_LABEL, KLASS_NOTE, badge } from '../data/site.js';

const groups = ['emr', 'hybrid', 'booking', 'adjacent', 'unclear'];
const byKlass = Object.fromEntries(groups.map(k => [k, vendors.filter(v => v.klass === k)]));
const plural = (n, w) => `${n} ${w}${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
---
<Base
  title="Med spa EMR vs booking software — which platforms actually have clinical charting"
  description={`Of ${vendors.length} med spa platforms, ${byKlass.emr.length} have genuine medical charting and ${byKlass.booking.length} have none at all. Which is which, and why buying the wrong one costs you twice.`}
  crumbs={['EMR or booking']}
>
<section class="ms-section">
  <p class="ms-eyebrow">Guide</p>
  <h1 class="ms-display">EMR or booking system?</h1>
  <p class="ms-lede ms-measure">
    The most expensive mistake in this category is buying a beautiful booking platform and
    discovering, after migration, that it cannot chart a treatment. These products are marketed
    with nearly identical language. They are not nearly identical.
  </p>
  <Stamp>Classifications are our editorial judgment applied to vendor documentation. <a href="/methodology/">How we decide</a>.</Stamp>
</section>

<section class="ms-section">
  <div class="ms-callout ms-callout-caution">
    <p class="ms-callout-title">Scope</p>
    <p>
      This page is about software capability, not clinical or legal advice. What your practice is
      required to document, who must supervise it, and which records you must retain are questions
      for your medical director and your state board — not for a software comparison site. We stay
      on the software.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ms-section">
  <h2 class="ms-h2">The distinction that matters</h2>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    Practically every platform here can take a booking, run a card and send a reminder text. The
    divide is what happens in the treatment room.
  </p>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    A <strong>clinical EMR</strong> records the procedure: structured or SOAP-style notes,
    injection maps, treatment-specific consent capture, before-and-after photography tied to the
    patient record, and usually e-prescribing. A <strong>booking and POS system</strong> records
    the transaction. It may offer intake forms and file attachments, which look adjacent to
    charting and are not the same thing.
  </p>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    If your practice performs injectables, energy-based treatments, or anything requiring a
    prescription, a booking-only platform means you will run a second system alongside it. That
    second system is a real line item, and it almost never appears in the comparison tables that
    put these products side by side.
  </p>
</section>

{groups.filter(k => byKlass[k].length).map(k => (
  <section class="ms-section">
    <p class="ms-kicker">{KLASS_LABEL[k]}</p>
    <h2 class="ms-h2">
      {plural(byKlass[k].length, 'platform')}
      {' '}<span class={badge(k)} style="vertical-align:middle">{KLASS_LABEL[k]}</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="ms-measure">{KLASS_NOTE[k]}</p>
    <div class="ms-scroller">
      <table class="ms-data">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Platform</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">From</th>
            <th scope="col">What we verified</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        {byKlass[k].map(v => (
          <tr>
            <td><span class="ms-cell-name"><a href={`/software/${v.slug}/`}>{v.displayName}</a></span></td>
            <td class="num num-strong">{v.startingPrice != null ? money(v.startingPrice) + '/mo' : <span class="nil">Quote</span>}</td>
            <td class="prose">{v.clinical}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
))}

<section class="ms-section">
  <h2 class="ms-h2">How to use this</h2>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    Work out which column you belong in before you shortlist, not after. Three questions settle it.
  </p>

  <h3 class="ms-h3">Does a licensed provider perform a procedure that must be documented?</h3>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    If yes, you need the clinical column — or a booking platform plus a separate EMR, budgeted as
    two subscriptions rather than one.
  </p>

  <h3 class="ms-h3">Does anyone prescribe?</h3>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    E-prescribing is a paid module almost everywhere it exists. Aesthetic Record charges $31–45 per
    prescriber depending on term; AestheticsPro bundles it only at the top tier. Price it
    separately rather than assuming it comes with the plan.
  </p>

  <h3 class="ms-h3">How many locations and how many providers?</h3>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    This decides more of your bill than the platform choice does. Per-location pricing punishes
    multi-site; per-user pricing punishes large teams.
    <a href="/cost-calculator/">Run both through the calculator.</a>
  </p>
</section>

{byKlass.unclear.length ? (
  <section class="ms-section">
    <div class="ms-callout">
      <p class="ms-callout-title">Where we would not trust a label</p>
      <p>
        {byKlass.unclear.length} platforms market clinical capability in terms we could not verify
        from public documentation — {byKlass.unclear.map(v => v.displayName).join(' and ')}. That is
        not an accusation; quote-only vendors reasonably keep detail behind a sales conversation.
        But we will not score a capability we have not been able to check, and neither should you.
        Ask for a charting demonstration using your own treatment types before signing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
) : null}
</Base>
